# Build context for the editor image, and the reason this file has to exist.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the root `.dockerignore`
# when one is present, and the two images need opposite things from the same
# repository:
#
#   deploy/hetzner-staging/Dockerfile builds flowstarter-main, and the root
#   `.dockerignore` rightly drops `apps/flowstarter-editor` from its context --
#   the editor is a whole second application and none of it ships in the app
#   image.
#
#   This Dockerfile builds the editor, and that same line made it unbuildable:
#   `pnpm --filter @flowstarter/editor-web build` answered "No projects matched
#   the filters in /app", then the `cp` of `web/dist` failed, because the only
#   thing missing from the context was the application being built. The header
#   of the Dockerfile says "the root .dockerignore already excludes
#   node_modules/dist/.git, so the build is hermetic", which was true of those
#   three and silently untrue of the app itself.
#
# So this list is the root one with that single line removed, plus the
# workspaces the editor genuinely does not need. Keep it in step with
# `.dockerignore` when that file changes; the parts that differ are marked.

.git
.github
.depot
.husky
.nx
.t3
.next
.turbo
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/.cache
**/*.log
.local
coverage
**/coverage
.tmp
tmp
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
artifacts
e2e
docs
flowstarter
readiness
supabase

# DIFFERENT FROM THE ROOT LIST: `apps/flowstarter-editor` is deliberately NOT
# excluded here. It is what this image builds.

# The other applications. None of them is compiled into the editor image, and
# pnpm is given explicit `--filter`s, so their absence costs nothing. Their
# package.json files stay so the lockfile's importers still resolve.
apps/flowstarter-main/**
!apps/flowstarter-main/package.json
apps/flowstarter-library/**
!apps/flowstarter-library/package.json
apps/flowstarter-templates/**
!apps/flowstarter-templates/*/package.json
apps/flowstarter-selfserve/**
!apps/flowstarter-selfserve/package.json
apps/shopify-landing/**
!apps/shopify-landing/package.json
apps/build-worker/**
!apps/build-worker/package.json
apps/deploy-agent/**
!apps/deploy-agent/package.json

# The shared packages are kept whole: `packages/platform-config` and its
# siblings are real dependencies of nothing in the editor today, but the
# lockfile names them and they are small. Dropping them would trade a few
# hundred kilobytes for a class of "works locally, fails in CI" install
# failure, which is not a trade worth making.
deploy
scripts
mprocs.yaml
ecosystem.config.cjs
playwright.config.ts
